OpenTyrian @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=====================================================

OpenTyrian is the open-source engine of Tyrian, the vertical shoot-'em-up.
This is its AmigaOS 3.x build for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with SDL 2
through GFOpenGPU. Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/ from gfopenrtg's main of
  2 November 2026 or later (the game's own 320x200 screen).
- AHI for sound. GFOpenInput for pads (lowlevel.library alone gives the
  joystick port).
- The Tyrian 2.1 game data (freeware, not in this archive): see
  data/ReadMe.txt.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x opentyrian-...lha Games:),
then put the Tyrian 2.1 data in the drawer's data drawer. Settings and
saves go to the drawer's User drawer, made on the first run.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the game's icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  opentyrian. Options: --no-sound, --no-joystick, --data=DRAWER.
- The game starts on a 320x200 screen of its own. Alt+Return switches to a
  window and back.
- Keys: the arrow keys move, Space fires, Return changes the rear gun's
  mode, Ctrl and Left Alt fire the sidekicks, P pauses, Escape opens the
  menu. The mouse moves the ship too. Pads: A fires, B changes mode, X and
  Y fire the sidekicks, Start opens the menu.
- Quit from the menus to keep the settings (Ctrl-C does not save them).

Licence
-------

OpenTyrian is GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING.txt); its source is at
https://github.com/opentyrian/opentyrian. The Tyrian 2.1 data is freeware
from its makers under its own terms and is not part of this archive. The
icons are drawn from OpenTyrian's own program icon.

